.TH QFW 7 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Concepts"
.SH NAME
qfw \- runtime framework for quantum service discovery and execution
.SH DESCRIPTION
QFw connects applications to quantum processing managers through DEFw service
discovery. A deployment may use site-owned services that outlive applications
or application-owned services created inside a scheduler allocation.
.PP
Applications prepare runtime state with
.BR qfw-setup (1),
inspect it with
.BR qfw-status (1),
launch through
.BR qfw-srun (1),
and release application-owned state with
.BR qfw-teardown (1).
For local runtime profiles,
.B qfw-setup
uses the same lifecycle engine as
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1)
and
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1),
and
.B qfw-teardown
stops the recorded application-owned instances. Persistent site directory,
DVM, and QPM components remain independently managed through
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1)
and
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Site installation and shared endpoints are described by
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5).
Resolver order and application-launch behavior are described by
.BR qfw-runtime.yaml (5).
Available QPM implementations are described by
.BR qfw-services.yaml (5).
.SH MANUAL SECTIONS
Commands are documented in section 1. Configuration formats use section 5.
Architecture and operational concepts use section 7.
